{"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"isSwiftSixLanguageMode","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","text":"Bool","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" { ","kind":"text"},{"text":"get","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" }","kind":"text"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"true","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" when built by a 6.0+ toolchain, which selects ","type":"text"},{"code":"Package@swift-6.0.swift","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"its per-target language-mode setting. Reported rather than assumed, because the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"difference is invisible from the outside and decides whether the concurrency","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"guarantees were checked or merely intended.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"This reads the ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"language mode","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":", not the toolchain: ","type":"text"},{"code":"#if swift(>=6.0)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" tests the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"former and ","type":"text"},{"code":"#if compiler(>=6.0)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" the latter, and they genuinely differ in this","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"package. On a 6.x toolchain the library and the examples are built in Swift 6","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"mode while the test target is deliberately still built in Swift 5 mode — the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"library and examples compile clean under full strict-concurrency 